        "heat_max": 60,
        "heat_dissipation_per_s": 3,
        "note": "The second biped of 16b cut AE.1: the Mk1's six sections, a little heavier everywhere (520 on the torso's front against 450), with the Mk1 thermal sight in its head at the thermal tank's 650 and 120. Doc 49 unit CC.3 (Q-49-6): the Mk1's 105 in the right arm as the main gun, the Mk1 laser in the left for drones and soft targets, and the machine gun in the torso; the cannon is listed first, so Class I's two slots arm it and the laser. The heat is the laser tank's: a 60 ceiling, 20 a pulse, 3 a second. It walks at 1,000 cm/s, twists at 40 degrees a second and backs at 40 per cent; it pays 200 for thick woods and 150 for rubble and climbs 70 per cent. It stands 11.5 m tall with the sight 9.5 m up. One leg gone is slow(50); both gone is disable_motion. Version 2 (17b cut M3.1): a line core in the torso. Version 3 (CC.3): the 105 beside the laser."
